    72	**Acceptance.**
    73	- Fixture ArcGIS server (injected responses, offline), per input: pages reassemble the layer with
    74	  the exact object-id set; duplicates, a missing page, a page error, a count mismatch, missing
    75	  pagination support, a wkid mismatch each refuse; `f=json` conversion of a point, a two-path
    26	| Merge trains, then a merge queue | 8 workers gave 10× activity for 2–3× merges; merges per worker-day fell from 5.6 to 0.3 at 18 workers | Squash merge on a green check; at most 2 coding lanes plus 1 records lane |
    27	| Nightly releases, release pinning, qualification | A night took 1 h 50 min at best, ARM64 70 min on the critical path; per-lane qualification 45 min serial | Every merge to main publishes the site; no version numbers |
    28	| Hardening lanes and a growing item list | 87 hardening merges against about 10 epic slices in a week; the list grew 150 → 217 | Defects under 50 lines ride on the next lane; a red main is reverted, not hardened |
    29	| Committed conformance results, locks, worker-check cron | Three lanes lost 30–45 min each on a dead lock; a queue stopped for an hour on a docs-only deadline | Nothing is committed that a job can regenerate; no locks; no cron |
    30	| Multiple Codex rounds, 4-revision caps | 2–4 h of a worker per round | One round for a kernel charter; none for surface or records |
    31	| Dispatch per commit group | Worth it for a 27-minute C++ build | A 2-minute check runs on every push; nothing to batch |
    32	| ccache, proven-tree skip, CI spend caps | Needed for a 27-minute C++ build | Irrelevant at Python-and-static scale; revisit above 10 min per check |
